WEBVTT

00:25.740 --> 00:27.570
"Police"

00:41.590 --> 00:47.050
<i>Let's chase our dreams...</i>

00:47.160 --> 00:52.130
<i>... holding hearts burning...</i>

00:52.200 --> 00:56.530
<i>... like the summer sunshine.</i>

00:56.640 --> 01:00.470
<i>If we have courage...</i>

01:00.570 --> 01:03.630
<i>... at 100 miles an hour...</i>

01:03.740 --> 01:11.740
<i>... I'm sure the door will open.</i>

01:11.850 --> 01:18.890
<i>Since sadness is the road</i>
<i>that leads to smiles...</i>

01:18.960 --> 01:27.600
<i>... dull, dingy shoes will</i>
<i>start to shine, too.</i>

01:27.700 --> 01:34.300
<i>The most wonderful dream</i>
<i>in the world...</i>

01:34.410 --> 01:41.010
<i>The pounding beat speeds up.</i>

01:41.110 --> 01:48.180
<i>The eyes are prisms that</i>
<i>catch the wind...</i>

01:48.290 --> 01:55.960
<i>... and in the voices of</i>
<i>countless friends...</i>

01:56.060 --> 02:02.800
<i>... I feel happiness.</i>

02:05.770 --> 02:08.670
FILE. 1
AND SO THEY MET

02:35.900 --> 02:39.170
As of this moment, fifteen minutes
late already, I see...

03:02.560 --> 03:03.550
I'll go for it.

03:42.240 --> 03:43.830
Let it slide! Please!

03:47.840 --> 03:50.610
I guess not, after all.
In that case...

04:09.400 --> 04:11.160
Whew...

04:11.260 --> 04:14.260
She couldn't have chased
me this far.

04:15.540 --> 04:17.470
N... No way...

04:26.110 --> 04:27.550
"Police"

04:29.120 --> 04:33.850
It ain't fair if all that counts is speed!
I'm gonna get caught!

04:34.390 --> 04:35.350
A temple?!

04:35.860 --> 04:36.880
My lucky day!

04:39.690 --> 04:41.350
Charge!

04:43.230 --> 04:44.590
Go! Go!

04:46.430 --> 04:49.600
I'm impressed. But it looks like
she's reached her limit.

04:49.700 --> 04:53.800
Heave! Heave! Heave-HO!

04:57.940 --> 04:59.970
NATSUMI POWER BOOST ON!

05:00.080 --> 05:03.210
DASH! Left-right! Left-right!

05:03.580 --> 05:04.780
Eh?!

05:04.880 --> 05:06.220
Fine!

05:14.460 --> 05:17.020
In hopes that I can do well
at my new workplace.

05:25.610 --> 05:30.270
Oshou! Oshou! You sure are
lively, considering the heat.

05:25.610 --> 05:30.070
"Oshou:" in Buddhism, the priest in charge of a temple.

05:30.380 --> 05:31.540
Oh, it's nothing.

05:31.640 --> 05:33.610
I'm in a hurry, so I'll
catch you later!

05:50.700 --> 05:53.530
Whew! I thought I was a goner.
What's the time?

05:53.630 --> 05:55.690
Nine... Wha?

06:14.590 --> 06:19.460
There! Hey, kitty, that was pretty
dangerous, you know!

06:19.560 --> 06:22.360
Even though you're lucky
it was me passing by...

06:22.460 --> 06:26.730
...you were on the verge of becoming
today's first accident fatality! Hmm?

06:27.400 --> 06:30.560
Oh! You're hungry,
huh? OK, OK...

06:32.510 --> 06:35.670
Huh? What?!

06:36.910 --> 06:39.670
Gone... It's gone...

06:40.380 --> 06:44.080
My lunch... My lunch!

06:46.120 --> 06:48.680
And now, the question;

06:51.060 --> 06:53.790
How many moving violations
did you commit?

06:54.160 --> 07:03.800
"Score:"

06:54.330 --> 06:55.660
Use of an area prohibited to motor traffic.

06:55.730 --> 06:57.530
Changing lanes in a no-passing zone.

06:57.600 --> 06:59.100
Disobeying traffic signs.

06:59.170 --> 07:01.530
Disregarding instructions of an officer.

07:01.600 --> 07:04.240
And... exceeding the speed limit, too.

07:03.900 --> 07:05.500
<i>"Suspension of License"</i>

07:05.610 --> 07:11.510
The posted legal speed is 30 kph, so
that puts you 25 kph over...

07:15.620 --> 07:18.780
...but in deference to kitty,
I'll let it slide.

07:18.890 --> 07:21.550
So if you would kindly
sign here...

07:21.650 --> 07:23.020
...Ms. Natsumi Tsujimoto!

07:23.760 --> 07:25.780
Huh? How do you
know my name?

07:27.460 --> 07:29.760
Welcome to Bokuto Precinct!

07:32.530 --> 07:34.860
"Bokuto Police Station"

07:35.170 --> 07:36.600
Natsumi Tsujimoto!

07:36.700 --> 07:37.400
Yes, sir!

07:37.570 --> 07:41.030
As of today, you are a policewoman
of Bokuto Precinct. Is that clear?

07:41.210 --> 07:41.430
Yes, sir!

07:41.610 --> 07:45.310
And on your first day of duty, you're
an hour and ten minutes late.

07:45.480 --> 07:45.970
Incorrect, sir.

07:46.150 --> 07:46.580
Hmm?

07:46.750 --> 07:49.080
An hour and twelve
minutes, sir.

07:49.250 --> 07:50.340
That's some nerve
you've got.

07:50.520 --> 07:52.420
People say that to me
all the time, sir!

07:52.590 --> 07:57.050
In any case, if you have an
excuse, I'll hear it. Well?

07:57.220 --> 07:58.320
Yes, sir, I do!

07:58.420 --> 08:03.260
The truth is, today, I actually got the
fried egg for lunch done really well.

08:03.360 --> 08:06.990
And when I went to give it to the old lady
next door, she was so psyched!

08:07.100 --> 08:09.330
She went on about how I just had
to become her grandson's bride.

08:09.440 --> 08:11.560
But her grandson is
still only seven...

08:11.670 --> 08:14.000
...so she gave me lots of pickled
vegetables by way of thanks...

08:14.110 --> 08:15.670
...and I was re-soaking them when
I looked at my watch...

08:15.780 --> 08:17.040
...and suddenly it was
eight o'clock!

08:17.140 --> 08:19.080
I raced like mad to get myself together,
and when I got on my RZ...

08:19.180 --> 08:21.270
...wouldn't you know it, the
engine wouldn't turn over!

08:21.380 --> 08:23.410
And it was just fine
yesterday, too!

08:23.520 --> 08:28.320
But that's A-OK! I have a Moto-Compo,
y'know! And it's in top condition!

08:28.420 --> 08:30.910
If I really pushed it, I'd be on time!
Am I lucky or what?!

08:31.020 --> 08:32.460
But I wasn't going to
get off that easily!

08:32.560 --> 08:34.420
No sooner did I hit Mito Boulevard,
then, of all things!

08:34.590 --> 08:37.650
Pun on "Mito Koomon," a famous TV samurai.
You ran into Lord Koomon's
entourage, I presume?

08:37.830 --> 08:43.600
Eh? Oh, wow. Making a joke that
far off must be a kind of genius, sir!

08:47.070 --> 08:47.970
And?

08:48.070 --> 08:52.140
At any rate, I, Natsumi Tsujimoto, was
late, but I will give my all for my duty.

08:53.080 --> 08:57.210
In the name of love, courage, and justice,
I will protect the people! That is all!

08:57.380 --> 09:00.650
All right! Welcome aboard!

09:00.820 --> 09:02.410
Oh, thank you.

09:03.290 --> 09:05.350
My fellow officers, I, Natsumi Tsujimoto...

09:05.460 --> 09:08.260
...hope that we will work
well together. Huh?

09:08.490 --> 09:12.120
As she says. I want you all to help
her out wherever necessary.

09:12.230 --> 09:13.820
Kobayakawa, come
here for a sec.

09:14.000 --> 09:15.230
Yes, sir.

09:16.540 --> 09:21.870
This is Miyuki Kobayakawa. She too was
just assigned here this past spring.

09:21.980 --> 09:24.470
Starting today, she will
be your partner.

09:24.640 --> 09:26.440
Miyuki Kobayakawa.
How do you do?

09:30.320 --> 09:32.050
Partner?!

09:36.460 --> 09:38.890
You've got real nerve.
I like that.

09:39.060 --> 09:40.420
Here we go...

09:40.590 --> 09:42.320
I'm getting to like it here, too.

09:42.430 --> 09:45.420
It looks like this is a happening
place, and it feels right to me.

09:45.600 --> 09:49.000
I like the way you talk. I'm Ken
Nakajima, motorcycle patrol.

09:49.100 --> 09:52.270
People call me the "White Hawk
of Bokuto." How do you!

09:56.310 --> 10:00.140
Nakajima, Yoriko, I have some things
to do, so take over for me, OK?

10:00.250 --> 10:04.440
Oh, I'll fix those binoculars
for you. Later...

10:04.880 --> 10:06.850
Uh, yeah...

10:08.320 --> 10:11.190
You see, Nakajima
has a thing for...

10:11.360 --> 10:13.020
I can hear you, Yoriko.

10:13.190 --> 10:13.890
Oops!

10:37.780 --> 10:40.120
There's too much you don't
know, Nakajima.

10:40.220 --> 10:40.740
Sorry.

10:40.920 --> 10:42.850
There seems to be
a lot to remember.

10:42.960 --> 10:47.360
Oh, excuse me for a sec. I've got to talk
about something. With my partner.

10:50.100 --> 10:53.090
Hey! What're you doing
to my bike?

10:54.270 --> 10:56.100
You wiped out pretty
badly this morning!

10:56.200 --> 10:59.230
The kickstarter was broken, and
you were leaking oil, too!

10:59.340 --> 11:02.710
Oh, I put in new wires
and plugs.

11:02.810 --> 11:05.210
Give it proper maintenance
from now on, OK?

11:05.310 --> 11:08.010
And I tinkered around with
various other things too...

11:08.110 --> 11:10.340
...but this time it's a special
job, on the house.

11:10.920 --> 11:13.650
Oh! I'm so lucky!

11:13.750 --> 11:18.420
...NOT! I mean, what's the big idea,
checking up on a person like that?

11:18.520 --> 11:20.360
How much do you
know about me?

11:21.130 --> 11:23.360
Let's see, career history,
special skills...

11:23.460 --> 11:26.360
...and performance evaluations from your
previous postings... as of now, that is.

11:26.900 --> 11:29.660
Is that all? Then you don't know about
when I was in school, and...

11:29.770 --> 11:31.740
...I worked my butt off to support
my motorbike hobby...

11:31.840 --> 11:33.930
...or that in school I was known
as the queen of tardiness...

11:34.040 --> 11:36.130
...and the eating monster...
Ah, I see, I see.

11:38.640 --> 11:40.640
I'll put that in your data file.

11:40.810 --> 11:45.810
Why are you going over my background
like that? What am I to you?

11:45.990 --> 11:48.220
My partner, of course.

12:00.400 --> 12:02.030
What're you looking
at, Nakajima?

12:02.200 --> 12:04.230
The birds. I'm bird watching.

12:04.400 --> 12:07.430
Oh? Birds are wearing uniforms
these days, eh?

12:07.610 --> 12:10.440
Wh... What are you talking
about, Yoriko?!

12:10.540 --> 12:12.510
It's not like I'm interested
in Kobaya!

12:13.710 --> 12:17.950
Aw, you're too easy to trip up, Nakajima.
It's just no fun at all.

12:18.380 --> 12:21.550
Do me a favor, and don't spread
any weird rumors, OK?

12:21.650 --> 12:23.050
I'm the tough guy, after all...

12:23.220 --> 12:25.120
The tough guy, huh?

12:46.650 --> 12:49.950
Starting today, we'll be in charge of the
area from Districts Three through Five.

12:50.050 --> 12:51.780
Two patrols a day, in the morning
and in the evening.

12:51.880 --> 12:54.940
In summertime, we work 'til six.
Oh, and by the way...

12:55.050 --> 12:58.020
...the basement cafeteria's "A" Lunch is
full of oysters, so that'd be my pick.

12:58.190 --> 12:59.780
I don't care for oysters.

12:59.960 --> 13:00.650
Oh, really?

13:00.830 --> 13:02.120
That and...

13:02.230 --> 13:04.060
...a certain someone
right in front of me.

13:05.260 --> 13:07.360
I know it's rude, but
I'm gonna be blunt.

13:07.470 --> 13:10.700
I don't think I can make
this work out with you.

13:10.800 --> 13:13.800
You're the type that gets picky about
data this and data that...

13:13.910 --> 13:16.500
...you crack down on traffic violations
like there was no tomorrow...

13:16.610 --> 13:18.100
...and to top it off, you meddle
in other people's affairs.

13:18.210 --> 13:20.080
You're completely
unlike me.

13:21.050 --> 13:25.450
Yeah, there may be no guarantees that
we'll become really good partners.

13:25.550 --> 13:31.820
But there is just one thing that I can
say with certainty; I'm really...

13:31.920 --> 13:35.830
...l'm really starting to like you.

13:48.340 --> 13:49.470
OK, then, let's do this...

13:51.110 --> 13:54.440
I'll toss this coin. If it comes up
tails, we'll talk to the Captain...

13:54.550 --> 13:58.540
...and have ourselves reassigned.
If it comes up heads...

13:58.720 --> 14:00.910
...I team up with you, huh?

14:11.900 --> 14:15.860
Our future... is in my hands...

14:30.980 --> 14:32.120
What was that?

14:32.120 --> 14:33.380
What was that?
Hold it, you!

14:36.960 --> 14:38.320
Let's go after him, too!

14:38.320 --> 14:39.520
Let's go after him, too!
Fine by me!

14:47.230 --> 14:51.170
Captain! A red Mini is racing through
the area! It's terrible!

14:51.340 --> 14:52.330
A red Mini...

14:52.870 --> 14:56.710
Nakajima, Kobayakawa, and
Tsujimoto are chasing it.

14:56.810 --> 14:58.240
We've got to send out backup!

14:58.410 --> 14:59.570
Don't worry about it.

14:59.750 --> 15:00.840
Huh?

15:01.210 --> 15:04.340
There'll be no danger from that
red Mini. We can let it be.

15:04.520 --> 15:06.850
Uh... yes, sir.

15:09.060 --> 15:12.680
You come along whenever
someone new shows up...

15:30.840 --> 15:34.300
Nice going! You took that corner
like nobody's business!

15:34.410 --> 15:36.110
But it looks like you're
out of luck.

15:36.220 --> 15:38.410
There's construction work up
ahead. It's a dead end!

15:47.130 --> 15:48.650
That was rude!

15:49.060 --> 15:50.030
Sand!

15:54.900 --> 15:55.920
Nakajima!

16:00.940 --> 16:02.410
Are you all right, Nakajima?

16:02.580 --> 16:05.570
Just putting on a little show!
Now get after him!

16:05.750 --> 16:07.040
Uh... right.

16:12.280 --> 16:14.150
I'm counting on you two.

16:16.820 --> 16:18.190
You bastard!

16:18.290 --> 16:21.020
You were waiting for
us? What a jerk!

16:21.190 --> 16:21.990
Unforgivable...

16:22.160 --> 16:23.220
Huh?

16:23.360 --> 16:29.670
I built that GSX-R specially... And
you go and make it wipe out...

16:29.770 --> 16:31.740
I'll get you if it's the
last thing I do!

16:35.640 --> 16:37.730
Fox calling Kittens.

16:37.910 --> 16:39.540
Fox? Who is this?

16:39.710 --> 16:41.440
The game has begun.

16:41.610 --> 16:43.080
It's the driver
of that Mini!

16:43.250 --> 16:47.350
In 120 minutes, fireworks
will go off at H8K2.

16:47.520 --> 16:49.650
Fireworks? You
can't mean!

16:49.820 --> 16:51.410
Is he talking about
a time bomb?

16:51.590 --> 16:56.460
Let's synchronize watches.
3... 2... 1...

16:57.600 --> 16:59.790
Hey! What the heck's H8K2?

16:59.970 --> 17:03.900
You will know that when all
the running around is over.

17:04.070 --> 17:05.230
What're you after?

17:05.400 --> 17:08.810
This is a salute to the establishment
of your new partnership.

17:08.970 --> 17:10.640
How do you know
about that?

17:10.810 --> 17:13.180
Besides, we still haven't decided
whether to BE partners!

17:13.350 --> 17:16.250
This is a game. Let's
enjoy ourselves!

17:16.420 --> 17:18.780
If you like, you can even
call for backup.

17:18.880 --> 17:20.180
If you lack confidence
in yourselves, that is.

17:20.350 --> 17:22.720
"Catch me by yourselves,"
is that it?

17:22.820 --> 17:27.590
You're on! We'll catch you long
before those two hours are up!

17:28.830 --> 17:31.060
Then I wish you luck.

17:33.400 --> 17:34.570
Don't lose him!

17:34.570 --> 17:35.560
Don't lose him!
I know, I know!

17:50.780 --> 17:52.340
He's heading for
the riverbed!

17:52.490 --> 17:54.180
Hold on tight, OK?

18:01.490 --> 18:03.190
What is it with that Mini?

18:03.330 --> 18:04.730
It's an ERA Turbo.

18:04.830 --> 18:06.730
From the outside, it's just a Mini
that's been modified a little.

18:06.830 --> 18:08.730
But it's a whole different
beast on the inside.

18:08.870 --> 18:09.600
What do you mean?

18:09.700 --> 18:11.570
I mean we're dealing with
a serious car nut.

18:11.740 --> 18:12.900
Then we can't beat him?

18:13.070 --> 18:15.510
Don't worry! This car's
no slouch, either!

18:15.670 --> 18:16.200
Wha?

18:16.310 --> 18:19.370
I've modified the Beat-type E-074
engine into a twin-cam type...

18:19.480 --> 18:21.500
...and upped the displacement
to 700cc.

18:21.610 --> 18:23.480
And with the turbo and
intercooler systems...

18:23.580 --> 18:26.950
...the maximum engine output exceeds
100 hp. And on top of that...

18:27.120 --> 18:27.920
"On top of that?"

18:28.090 --> 18:30.180
There's a custom-made
nitro injector, too!

18:30.360 --> 18:31.980
"Nitro?!"

18:32.160 --> 18:34.350
Nitro! On!

18:36.800 --> 18:38.460
We're gonna catch you!

18:45.540 --> 18:47.700
You tell people not to speed,
but just look at you!

18:47.870 --> 18:51.070
If they run, I chase them.
It's my job, after all.

18:51.540 --> 18:52.840
You're all right.

18:57.020 --> 18:58.070
You're not getting away!

19:39.760 --> 19:42.520
Damn! Y... You're good!

19:42.700 --> 19:43.490
Now's our chance!

19:43.660 --> 19:44.630
Huh?

19:46.930 --> 19:50.030
There's a high school up ahead.
The road takes a big detour.

19:50.140 --> 19:52.330
If we play our cards right, we
can catch him in a pincer!

19:52.500 --> 19:54.470
Which means it's time for
this baby's entrance.

19:59.210 --> 20:00.510
Let's do it!

20:02.410 --> 20:05.110
This baby's smoking! She
really is something!

20:05.220 --> 20:06.180
Now I'm set!

20:11.320 --> 20:12.350
Coming through!

20:13.560 --> 20:15.360
And... take that!

20:16.730 --> 20:18.890
Nice shot, sweetie!

20:21.270 --> 20:23.860
Checkmate! The game
is over, Mr. Fox!

20:30.140 --> 20:33.110
This area is closed to traffic.
My condolences!

20:35.610 --> 20:38.810
You can't get away now!
Give yourself up!

20:44.820 --> 20:46.120
WHAT?!

20:46.660 --> 20:48.060
N... Natsumi! Get him!

20:48.230 --> 20:49.320
I'm on it!

21:07.350 --> 21:08.900
Only thirty minutes left.

21:09.080 --> 21:10.880
It's all over, I guess.

21:12.250 --> 21:14.150
The game of tag ends here.

21:14.250 --> 21:18.550
You both did well. As a reward,
I'll give you a hint.

21:18.660 --> 21:24.890
The code name of your goal is "Emily."
Study your information once more.

21:25.000 --> 21:26.620
Give it everything you've got.
That is all.

21:27.630 --> 21:29.760
"Emily?" A girl?

21:30.000 --> 21:33.600
What did he mean by that? I'm
no good at this kind of thing!

21:33.770 --> 21:36.330
Calm down, Miyuki.
Try to remember...

21:36.440 --> 21:39.500
He said we'd understand when all
the running around was done...

21:39.610 --> 21:43.050
When all the running
around was done...

21:43.150 --> 21:44.120
That's it!

21:44.220 --> 21:46.650
Have you figured
something out?

21:47.250 --> 21:51.350
Look! I've drawn a line through
the roads we chased him over.

21:51.520 --> 21:53.390
Isn't this... an airplane?

21:59.100 --> 22:03.630
Serial number H8K2, code name "Emily,"
refers to the Type Two Flying Boat.

22:03.740 --> 22:06.230
Built in 1940, it was tops in the world
during WWll when it came to...

22:06.340 --> 22:10.140
...speed, flight range, and waterborne
takeoffs and landings!

22:10.310 --> 22:12.040
What's that got to do
with anything?

22:12.140 --> 22:14.510
There still is one now...
at Odaiba Park.

22:17.320 --> 22:18.180
Only twenty minutes to go!

22:18.280 --> 22:21.880
We'll never make it using normal
roads. Find us a short cut!

22:21.990 --> 22:23.110
OK!

22:25.390 --> 22:29.490
There's a subway tunnel under
construction 500m ahead!

22:29.600 --> 22:33.220
If we cut through there, it puts us directly
on Expressway Nine... the Bayshore!

22:33.330 --> 22:34.630
Roger!

22:49.080 --> 22:50.080
Ten minutes!

22:50.080 --> 22:50.980
Ten minutes!
We gotta make it!

23:02.190 --> 23:03.530
There it is... by the landing gear!

23:03.700 --> 23:05.460
Everyone! Please evacuate!

23:05.630 --> 23:06.500
This is dangerous! Please evacuate!

23:06.500 --> 23:07.120
This is dangerous! Please evacuate!
What?

23:07.230 --> 23:07.330
They said it's dangerous!

23:07.330 --> 23:08.860
They said it's dangerous!
Please get out of here!

23:08.970 --> 23:09.400
Hurry! Please get out of here!

23:09.400 --> 23:10.700
Hurry! Please get out of here!
Only thirty seconds left!

23:10.800 --> 23:11.960
Look, you get out of here, too!

23:12.140 --> 23:12.540
Huh?

23:12.700 --> 23:16.330
I can defuse this old thing.
So get out of here!

23:16.510 --> 23:21.040
Miyuki! Even for you, it's impossible!
I'll throw this thing in the ocean!

23:21.180 --> 23:22.310
That's impossible, too!

23:22.480 --> 23:24.780
How many meters do you think
it is to the ocean from here?

23:24.880 --> 23:25.780
You can't throw it that far!

23:25.950 --> 23:26.950
Look, let me handle it!

23:26.950 --> 23:28.080
Look, let me handle it!
Get your hands out of the way!

23:28.190 --> 23:29.920
We're running out of time!

23:30.090 --> 23:31.280
Time?

23:37.200 --> 23:38.700
Wow! That's pretty!

23:38.700 --> 23:39.660
Wow! That's pretty!
Fireworks?

23:47.740 --> 23:51.200
"Game Over; If found, please
report to the police?"

23:47.740 --> 23:52.340
"From Fox to Kittens"

23:51.380 --> 23:52.740
Oh! I just
bet!

23:55.580 --> 23:59.020
It is! It's my lunch! I'm happy!

24:00.050 --> 24:03.180
Oh, is that all?

24:06.660 --> 24:08.350
How green.

24:24.210 --> 24:27.540
We went through a lot today... but
didn't it seem pretty interesting...

24:27.650 --> 24:29.240
...when all's said and done?

24:29.410 --> 24:31.540
Well, it wasn't boring,
that's for sure...

24:31.720 --> 24:36.620
Hmph. You certainly looked like you
were enjoying yourself, though.

24:36.790 --> 24:42.120
Yes, ma'am. Thanks to my top notch
partner, it was an enjoyable day.

24:42.290 --> 24:44.090
Now that's more like it.

24:44.200 --> 24:47.500
Hey, Partner, are you interested
in moving?

24:47.670 --> 24:48.690
Moving?

24:48.870 --> 24:52.000
Your present apartment is far away
and inconvenient, right?

24:52.100 --> 24:55.340
There's a nice place, very close
to Bokuto Precinct.

24:55.440 --> 25:00.540
Lots of sunshine, and a pretty,
punctual roommate, to boot.

25:00.650 --> 25:03.620
Are you by any chance suggesting
we live together?

25:03.720 --> 25:06.340
You'd benefit by not being
late anymore.

25:06.520 --> 25:07.950
What's your real motive?

25:08.120 --> 25:11.520
It's kinda unsafe for a woman
to be living alone, you know!

25:11.690 --> 25:13.520
What does that make me?

25:13.690 --> 25:15.060
My bodyguard!

25:16.460 --> 25:20.360
Oh, no! And I've still got
lunch left over, too!

25:20.530 --> 25:22.360
Okay, say ah!

25:22.530 --> 25:23.560
Ah!

25:27.740 --> 25:29.710
Salty! What is this?

25:34.880 --> 25:36.750
W... Why you...

25:45.690 --> 25:48.250
By the way, what was the outcome
of that coin toss?

25:48.360 --> 25:50.260
Oh! I completely forgot.

25:50.400 --> 25:51.330
Let me do it.

25:51.500 --> 25:53.560
Sure. I'll leave it up to you.

25:53.730 --> 25:54.930
Thank you.

25:57.440 --> 25:59.100
OK then, here I go.

25:59.270 --> 26:00.360
Be my guest.

26:02.310 --> 26:10.240
How about THIS?!

26:25.200 --> 26:33.540
<i>I love the smile you always have.</i>
<i>With all the passion I have...</i>

26:33.610 --> 26:42.940
<i>... I will protect you from sighs.</i>

26:43.050 --> 26:50.890
<i>The sunset skyline flashes past</i>
<i>in my side-view mirror.</i>

26:50.960 --> 26:58.450
<i>This is the road I drive on every day,</i>
<i>believing in my dreams.</i>

26:58.560 --> 27:06.360
<i>On rainy days, windy days, and days</i>
<i>when I wanted to throw it all away...</i>

27:06.470 --> 27:14.200
<i>... you smiled as you</i>
<i>sat beside me.</i>

27:15.480 --> 27:19.990
<i>I love the unchanging vista, the sky</i>
<i>that we watch together.</i>

27:23.990 --> 27:30.800
<i>That's why I'm confident that I can</i>
<i>hang in there, if it's for you.</i>

27:30.860 --> 27:39.270
<i>I love the smile you always have.</i>
<i>With all the passion I have...</i>

27:39.370 --> 27:39.500
<i>... I will protect you from sighs.</i>

27:45.840 --> 27:45.880
<i>I love this town where we</i>
<i>happened to meet...</i>

28:09.130 --> 28:13.370
It's coming... it's coming...
There's a storm coming!

28:13.540 --> 28:17.000
S... So you're the type that gets excited
when a typhoon comes too, huh?

28:17.110 --> 28:17.910
Oh, brother!

28:18.080 --> 28:20.840
Well, of course! Water flooding,
storms thrashing...

28:21.010 --> 28:22.540
...trees falling along streets, people
crashing into windows!

28:22.650 --> 28:24.950
Streets without people!
Slippery roads!

28:25.050 --> 28:28.880
And with things flying all over, danger
everywhere, it's such a joy!

28:28.990 --> 28:30.450
Er... hello?

28:30.560 --> 28:33.620
You're Under Arrest, File 2,
"Tokyo Typhoon Rally."

28:33.730 --> 28:36.630
FILE. 2
TOKYO TYPHOON RALLY

28:33.730 --> 28:36.630
Looks like there're others
just like you!
